Team Leader Habit Tracker Anti-Backtracking Rule and Rollout Plan: Carl specified that the team leader daily tracker must function as a gamified habit tracker that explicitly prevents back-tracking, ensuring team leaders log activities on the exact day they occur to eliminate procrastination, bulk-auditing, and cramming. Wes confirmed adjusting data entry fields to exclude manual date inputs so the tool captures only real-time entries. Jian will build the AppScript once Wes, Hez, and Roel finalize the specifications, leading to a planned two-week rollout period for team leaders.
Tracker Design Delivery Target and Future Analytics: Wes set a delivery target date of tomorrow to lock in the initial design specifications for the team leader daily tracker, drawing inspiration from Apple Health and Samsung Health profiles to display daily coaching and task completion scores. Jian will subsequently implement advanced backend analytics to evaluate team leader productivity patterns across different days of the week. Finally, Carl addressed asynchronous feedback on the action registry, projected effective usage visibility for the fourth quarter, and concluded the meeting.


